they'll make a girl of promise if you  know you can't keep it  hallo the Master Chief collection is an  infamous example of one of Microsoft's  blunders this console generation what  should have been an easy win as a  celebration of their biggest franchise  went sour after massive launch issues  that plagued everything from multiplayer  to the campaigns patches fixed the large  problems but the Master Chief collection  was never fully fixed to a level that  both the fans and three-for-three  themselves were happy with so it's kind  of insane that now almost four years  later 343 is returning to deliver a  massive update this summer promising an  overhaul to the matchmaking and visual  changes so to understand why this is  such a big deal we need to look back at  just how much of a mess the Master Chief  collection was at launch and how three  four three plans to fix it back at e3  2014 343 announced halo the Master Chief  collection it would poured over halo one  two three and four to the Xbox one and  get them running at 1080p 60 frames a  second  halo 2 would get remastered visuals the  same way halo combat Evolved did three  years earlier and perhaps most  meaningful of all all of these games  multiplayers would come over as well not  only could you seamlessly switch from a  match in Halo 3 to halo 4  but halo tubes multiplayer would return  after the original Xbox Live shutdown in  2010 and halo ones multiplayer would be  available on Xbox Live for the first  time this was an incredible value and  should have been a strong start to Halo  4 this console generation however once  the game was released problems cropped  up almost immediately for starters right  out launched there was no dedicated  playlist available for halo combat  Evolved 343 said they were holding off  until network performance for that  particular game was running smooth they  should have been a warning sign for  things to come as it quickly became a  minor point when matchmaking issues  began to crop up for every game in the  collection our Plus long wait times for  matches or failing to connect at all  became common for a lot of people other  issues extended into the campaign such  as in game freezes audio issues and  other bugs documented by fans it wasn't  a promising start but 343 responding  quickly with a number of server-side  updates to improve matchmaking days  after launch along with an apology from  the head of the studio these  improvements however were inconsistent  working on some players with others  still stuck in long matchmaking loading  times in a blog update just four days  after launch it was stated that recent  patches had shown a 20% increase in  server connectivity and that larger  issues would be fixed in a patch planned  for release on the 19th and yet despite  the massive list of issues this patch  was supposed to correct large number of  players didn't feel the effects and  we're still stuck without being able to  connect reliably what's worse is the  patch even added new UI bugs so fast  forward a few weeks in several apologies  later in a brand new patch is released  designed to finally fix the issues the  previous patch didn't and this one  actually stuck fixing a whole host of  matchmaking issues and getting things in  a stable state they were even able to  bring back playlist modes like SWAT  which had been removed right after  launch in an effort to help with  matchmaking finally a month after launch  the Master Chief collection was a  reliable product not perfect mind you  there was still a whole host of issues  and patches were regularly pushed out  all the way up until April 2015 but  despite all these improvements that  broke in first month severely hurt the  Master Chief collection z' reputation  many left before the game was fixed into  a playable state and even after it was  playable the damage was already done in  an effort to make it up to the fans  three-for-three added for free both halo  4 Spartan Ops mode and the entire  campaign of Halo 3 ODST the latter of  which was never originally planned for  the collection but was high on the list  of what fans wanted and made a very good  worse re-gift eventually things calm  down with the Master Chief collection  and once halo fives release began to  ramp up the update slowed down and  eventually stopped the Master Chief  collection became a painful mark on  343's history with Frank O'Connor  calling it a black eye for the studio  343 promised every future Halo game  would have a beta and more extensive  testing to make sure this never happened  again there's no real way of knowing  what the population of the collection  was like in the years sense there are  those hardcore fans that stuck with it  and played regularly and you have the  occasional fan that would pop in for a  match every once in a while  plateless ended up feeling a little  sparse and unreliable though you had a  much better chance of getting into a  match in team Slayer than you did on  just the halo 1 playlist where there  were kind of like the same ten people  over and over again but while the game  has been largely fixed and in good shape  for years there are still lingering  issues back in January of 2017 community  manager Brian jarred said on reddit that  conversations were still being had at  the studio about the possibility of  future updates that opportunity came in  the form of the launch of the Xbox one X  Microsoft's updated console that  supports 4k in October of 2017 three  years after the game's release 343  announced the Master Chief collection  would be getting an Xbox 1x enhanced  update it was looking at when we look at  Xbox 1x it's an opportunity to take our  current gen portfolio and enhance it  across to give a better play experience  that looks better on everything we're  doing and matched a massive collection  should definitely be part of that so  this is the time that we're going to  crack it open move it over to the latest  game operating system which has amazing  improvements to matchmaking which will  benefit from and now it's the right time  and we're pretty excited that we're  gonna move the whole portfolio forward  On January 31st 2018 Brian Jared also  known as sketch started a series of  development blogs on the Master Chief  collection update project if you're  someone who is interested in this update  these are definitely worth reading as  343 is very open and transparent on the  development and their plans for the  update on the backend the game's  matchmaking api's will be updated to the  current standard of xbox live which  should improve overall matchmaking and  make parties more reliable this will  also require an update to the  collections 8 separate engines so that  4k support and other visual enhancements  can be made there are also plenty of  exciting features to look forward to  such as Xbox 1x support including 4k  resolution and HDR offline land support  the ability to install each game  individually for those that only prefers  some of the games or have a restrictive  bandwidth there also updating the UI  with a brand new title screen and main  menu to take advantage of 4k and tweak  it for a better user experience all of  this plus a bunch of smaller  quality-of-life improvements such as a  replacement of the voting system which  is meant to address the issue of  everyone voting for only  three maps right now and 343 is planning  for further updates in the future such  as adding a custom game browser akin to  how halo seee  and halo to work on PC they've even  asked people what new features they'd  want to see in future updates the  biggest request being Halo Reach and ODS  T's firefight mode and while these  aren't planned for this current update  or even confirmed to be happening 343  has made it clear that they are aware  people want this and are looking into  the possibilities the other thing people  have been asking for years is for the  Master Chief collection to make its way  to PC which was given a similar response  however an interesting wrinkle in all  this is the recent drama around halo  online which actually happened during  the middle of editing this video the  short version is back in 2015 Microsoft  put out a closed beta for a free-to-play  version of Halo threes multiplayer in  Russia known as halo online the game was  cancelled in August of 2016 El Dorado is  a mod that has been keeping the game  alive removing the region barrier and  continuing to tweak and improve it being  built using microsoft own assets the  recent popularity of el dorado prompted  microsoft to start sending takedown  notices and even bans on twitch in  youtube obviously this didn't go over  well with the community and it's clear  from the popularity and outcry over el  dorado along with official releases like  halo 5 forge showing that there is a  large audience that wants halo 4 the PC  and three for three's official response  they said one thing remains clear the  community really wants more halo on PC  as we look ahead we're very excited  about the prospects of an official  classic halo experience making its way  to PC and we hope we'll be able to  partner with the eldorado team and  broader mod and content creation  community to help inform the types of  experiences and features our fans desire  while we have nothing to announce today  please know that the PC community is  very important to us and top of mind as  we work towards the future that part was  actually tweeted by the head of Xbox  Phil Spencer so all of this points to  ain't in the works project to bring  classic halo to pc whether this means  bringing the Master Chief collection to  PC or something else entirely is pure  speculation but the timing of all this  plus the summer release date for the  Master Chief collection update makes it  hard to not put two and two together but  regardless of all that this  is clearly more than a simple update  adding Xbox 1x support the amount of  effort put towards this update shows  that 343 really cares about fixing the  game and Microsoft still considers halo  and important enough of a property to  let them do it it's also a statement on  the way games are being treated nowadays  publishers and developers are sticking  the games longer adding new content and  improving the experience something that  started as a failure can still be turned  around  who knows if that'll be the case with  the Master Chief collection though again  this update is coming out almost four  years after its release and while I'm  sure there'll be a bump in the player  count when the update launches who knows  how long those people will actually  stick around for the patch is currently  being tested by members of the community  in a closed alpha referred to as a  flight so we'll start to get an idea  soon on how the hardcore fans feel about  it  30,000 people signed up for the flight  program which compared to a lot of the  big games nowadays shows how small halos  community has gotten you also have to  start to wonder how the eventual halo 6  will play into all this with the Master  Chief collection halo 5 + halo 6 the  halo community will be stretched pretty  thin you have to wonder even with all  this effort if it's really gonna do much  for the Master Chief collection halo as  a whole is in a really weird place right  now and it's hard to say for certain  what the future of the series will be  but I have to commend 343 for being  persistent in fixing their mistakes and  being open and transparent with their  community they're on the right path and  maybe just maybe 343 and Microsoft can  turn one of their biggest blunders this  generation into a success but we won't  find out until the update releases later  this summer go make a girl of promise  if you know you can't keep  [Music]
 

